(* Module: matplotlib.pyplot provides procedural plotting interface.) Tj
T*
(* Object-Oriented Hierarchy: Figure \(overall canvas window\) contains one or more Axes) Tj
T*
(\(individual subplots with coordinate systems\).) Tj
T*
(* Plot Primitives:) Tj
T*
(- plt.plot\(x, y, label, color, linestyle, marker\): Line charts \(continuous physical) Tj
T*
(signals\).) Tj
T*
(- plt.scatter\(x, y\): Discrete data points, correlation analysis.) Tj
T*
(- plt.bar\(categories, values\): Categorical comparisons.) Tj
T*
(- plt.hist\(data, bins\): Frequency probability distributions.) Tj
T*
(* Styling & Annotations: plt.title\(\), plt.xlabel\(\), plt.ylabel\(\), plt.grid\(True\),) Tj
T*
(plt.legend\(\), plt.xlim\(\), plt.ylim\(\), plt.tight_layout\(\), plt.savefig\("plot.png",) Tj
T*
(dpi=300\).) Tj
T*
